# Protect the ownership rules themselves.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @steipete

# Go gateway and build infrastructure.
/gateway-go/ @steipete
/Makefile @steipete

# WARNING: GitHub CODEOWNERS uses last-match-wins semantics.
# The security-sensitive rules live BELOW the broad rules above so they win the
# match (a broad rule listed after a narrow one silently strips its reviewers —
# the previous layout had /gateway-go/ after the secops block, which disabled
# the auth rule). If you add broader overlapping rules below this block,
# include @deneb/secops on those entries too.
# (The former /gateway-go/internal/infra/auth/ package was split into
# clientauth/ + secret/ + config/; all three keep auth-sensitive code —
# config/ resolves gateway tokens/passwords and enforces the
# no-auth-no-nonloopback-bind rule.)
/.github/dependabot.yml @deneb/secops
/.github/workflows/codeql.yml @deneb/secops
/gateway-go/internal/infra/clientauth/ @deneb/secops
/gateway-go/internal/infra/secret/ @deneb/secops
/gateway-go/internal/infra/config/ @deneb/secops
/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json @deneb/secops
